{
  "id": "torsion-free-group-algebra-with-zero-divisors",
  "title": "A torsion-free group algebra with zero divisors",
  "description": "There is a finitely presented torsion-free group G, with a finite two-dimensional classifying space, whose group algebra over the field with two elements has zero divisors: Kaplansky's zero-divisor conjecture fails. Two random immersed labelled graphs with prescribed letter sets of odd intersections, built from the projective plane over the field with 128 elements, make every contribution to a product cancel in pairs; a word-counting estimate, planar separation and cone pictures show that the group of the graphs is torsion-free and that the factors are nonzero. The course is an exposition of OpenAI's proof (2026).",
